{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--5477f471-713e-56d7-a46d-0e6c10ce1305","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-action--6","attack-action--7","attack-action--8","attack-action--9","attack-action--10","attack-action--11","attack-action--12","attack-action--13","attack-action--14","attack-action--15","attack-condition--1","attack-condition--2","attack-condition--3","attack-condition--4","attack-operator--1","software--postgres-monitor-service","instance--3536a568-610f-5570-bba9-6dfe97bc9c2e","instance--384798bd-a84b-5feb-8d38-7f9d0a087f11","instance--057c9c6b-5f9d-5a42-a700-338d5f0eb74a","instance--b6d82c28-0a68-5c6f-b058-c1e072f51852","instance--895aab9a-87c3-51d8-91f8-cc3f6dd1a5a5","instance--3bb881aa-a5ab-51ba-b53d-89d26964ce7d","instance--281f3c85-575b-56bd-9eb8-e244a2386e14","instance--02e57dc2-5a22-5e3f-9848-0ca55cc8cf86","instance--c075f5c6-95e8-5553-8f7e-b432b96021c7","instance--210c59c2-7864-58f4-9241-0b23bd868ab6","instance--4a5ea725-c4a7-5df9-9998-686e551226c2","instance--88f25f85-b4d1-57cb-9c54-8afff5236c3b","instance--b11f9060-9631-5fd8-a6d2-dff35ec92e04","instance--afab344e-9d8c-5f53-9094-3c4e35082ca0","instance--537e0171-dd9b-5009-8a9d-3789ba3ac707","instance--3c3df871-63db-5341-bea2-d06a0bdc4c20","instance--e6daf184-6d66-5f3a-acad-18184be6b9df","instance--f189558f-58f4-5824-9b6e-9eba8341eba5","instance--6668b31a-6646-571b-8f37-a2ebedaf10ba","instance--3378aaef-ea25-56a3-ac22-3cacbbf8f0aa"],"properties":[["name","TeamPCP CanisterWorm Iran payload flow"],["description","A TeamPCP payload chain that downloads and executes a staged payload, fingerprints Kubernetes and Iranian locale/timezone targets, deploys destructive or persistence DaemonSets, and in a later variant spreads via SSH and exposed Docker APIs."],["scope","campaign"],["author",[["name","Charlie Eriksen"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","www.aikido.dev"],["url","https://www.aikido.dev/blog/teampcp-stage-payload-canisterworm-iran"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Download and execute staged payload"],["description","What you can see is that it downloads if it's not already installed. Then it downloads from the same host, and executes that, before then deleting itself."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Detect Kubernetes pod environment"],["description","The first thing the payload does is figure out where it's running. Two checks:\n\nStandard Kubernetes pod detection. Every pod gets a service account mounted by default."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0007","technique":"T1082"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Check timezone and locale"],["description","It checks the system timezone and locale. If the machine is configured for Iran ( , , or ), the payload takes a very different path."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0007","technique":"T1614"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Deploy wiping DaemonSet"],["description","The Iranian-targeted DaemonSet is called . The container inside it is named . Subtle, this is not.\n\n\r\n\nThe DaemonSet mounts the host's root filesystem to , deletes everything at the top level, then force reboots. Because it's a DaemonSet with , it gets scheduled on every node in the cluster, including the control plane. One and the entire cluster is bricked."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0040","technique":"T1485"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Deploy backdoor DaemonSet"],["description","For non-Iranian targets, the DaemonSet ( ) is less dramatic but more operationally useful. It writes the CanisterWorm backdoor to every node and registers it as a systemd service:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1543.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Poll ICP canister for binary URL"],["description","The backdoor is the same one we documented in the CanisterWorm post. It polls the ICP canister every 50 minutes for a binary URL, downloads and executes whatever it's told. The kill switch is still present."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1102.003"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--7cccbcd0-a724-54fb-be4f-ac523d26f7d0","120":"instance--738e44b2-1357-5eb3-82bd-8a0ce8942b72","150":"instance--d31f4735-6339-5929-8d7c-d30863cf166f","180":"instance--2252393d-d801-5931-ad38-4b53374a9880","210":"instance--065b5ad5-023a-5336-b458-e9c9dcda2976","240":"instance--5ea0dd2b-5eac-51f8-855a-4cbcb801bc2d","270":"instance--bba66874-a069-56c6-bb95-967cb3cefc9e","30":"instance--6377c09d-ecb4-5567-a2f4-4dde56ff4f98","300":"instance--ede3430f-b16b-58ae-be71-1d1f1a194336","330":"instance--7772f482-8ee2-569a-b600-7528c065d4e0","60":"instance--98139a98-16b0-54fe-8c77-3473c1b520cd","90":"instance--5cb9cc95-e190-5a68-985d-0a94d39299e6"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--7","properties":[["name","Wipe non-Kubernetes Iranian hosts"],["description","For non-Kubernetes Iranian systems, the approach is cruder:\n\nIf it's root, it wipes the system. If not, it tries passwordless sudo, then tries anyway. Even without root, it'll destroy everything the user owns."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0040","technique":"T1485"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--5150f7cc-6f25-5eb3-a6fc-5099ced4caf4","120":"instance--64a408ce-c543-55d6-a9dd-206ce7cadbb2","150":"instance--1b71e413-cfd2-528c-8792-dc7dd1bb9938","180":"instance--aa12ce11-0165-52b6-b72d-e4d9070e9fbb","210":"instance--5d8b0f08-14bc-58f4-9316-b25a92dd09a6","240":"instance--34f96b84-9453-53f2-ae07-d28c04665e6c","270":"instance--415f1d54-1cd4-5ba7-8071-4aa99bc946ac","30":"instance--18834cac-b4c4-57b0-88ea-5a62fdb27cf9","300":"instance--de4f9957-1ac6-5782-86ea-f1a3b6a9ad13","330":"instance--8eff940b-86bb-556f-8c85-c7c47577b3ed","60":"instance--14a123fd-5626-5e69-8257-6dcd64c28ec0","90":"instance--02294ff1-7261-5db8-8e0d-b9e818922053"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--8","properties":[["name","Scan local subnet for targets"],["description","It also scans the local /24 subnet for new targets."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0007","technique":"T1018"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--180f2983-9c1a-56f4-99d6-c990125f7baa","120":"instance--c7f65318-7600-57f4-a8ac-992357e695ff","150":"instance--95523e1a-0a1d-52ef-944c-23f9cbc50233","180":"instance--bc8eb48d-411d-5877-aa9b-966476b71207","210":"instance--4cc5026e-07f9-5327-9912-5d278a0a3321","240":"instance--d6a7d51d-39a4-5eb3-8831-f23437781b95","270":"instance--cac30e05-5f01-5b4f-b5c0-6b975297df2d","30":"instance--cb0751b0-c027-5895-a460-a72e48920c71","300":"instance--f41cdc1f-abb7-5ff7-81c2-bf2235a7faab","330":"instance--b114cbda-9ec8-5612-b2f8-93c36811cafb","60":"instance--f28e5296-2041-5fe9-992d-4c70d549191e","90":"instance--3ea39244-da0f-5435-8745-f2afa8b13872"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--9","properties":[["name","Parse SSH auth logs"],["description","It parses and for successful SSH logins, extracting both the username and source IP. Those become targeted spreading pairs. For any IP it finds on the subnet that wasn't in the auth logs, it falls back to trying , , , and ."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0009","technique":"T1005"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--db5fab04-54d4-5eec-a429-185861eb2719","120":"instance--985391bd-d017-5935-ab31-3b4b56331b02","150":"instance--092bb98d-fc30-5f69-b6b7-e3024f3ec65a","180":"instance--755129e6-612e-5b63-a780-1c886d98909b","210":"instance--431723d9-dd8c-5190-9dab-6f346173c044","240":"instance--5b9fb821-54fe-5f22-bba3-038263245910","270":"instance--3c6777cb-6430-544b-b31a-01b198524553","30":"instance--c070071b-a9a3-52fe-8956-a51744db200b","300":"instance--a9a4289c-d995-5783-9544-a8b45052eb56","330":"instance--344009cc-e024-5c68-9246-51e85e00d45c","60":"instance--86c77621-2c1d-59c3-b398-e62f4b48a3dd","90":"instance--67627b08-1913-5f3d-8318-52d3bda9c1c3"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--10","properties":[["name","Steal SSH private keys"],["description","Then it grabs every SSH private key it can find:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0006","technique":"T1552.004"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--6b7baffd-afaf-5472-9af2-a263119a77ef","120":"instance--83f38e63-e29a-53f4-99d9-927a195c453f","150":"instance--3e720145-b7a1-5bd6-8a7d-bb13519675d1","180":"instance--bdce060f-d96c-5b06-b8f4-1ab1527fd01d","210":"instance--a4feb251-e6e3-5680-a712-d59c92f73ccf","240":"instance--9a564ca6-b753-5b06-880c-b3aac25c1e73","270":"instance--76861a89-f006-5e0d-8c5b-ebdcb5e926dc","30":"instance--cf41e64d-4a4b-58d9-9962-72d278b2c489","300":"instance--ac1d6edd-482f-5f13-9348-b605afcc260c","330":"instance--ed78dfa1-f300-564f-b2cd-6c99552b9a68","60":"instance--979accb3-1b3e-5af4-9182-78392cbaf904","90":"instance--ae721c42-320e-5ea4-9c77-339a05b6e12f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--11","properties":[["name","Spread over SSH"],["description","For each target, it checks two ports. Port 22 gets the SSH spread:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0008","technique":"T1021.004"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--f1e35721-7ac2-54fe-bcf6-5456d2faeaa3","120":"instance--3ff6777e-fcba-5b31-bf0f-3ddf77f6030d","150":"instance--cc6192f9-21a5-5d1a-b954-6a52d989b82d","180":"instance--62a87260-0181-5f49-bc05-733216e4d822","210":"instance--2f2d05c5-8e60-5ac2-b7af-e03027d67957","240":"instance--79c1ec18-d792-5d3d-a7bc-d94fe8b124cf","270":"instance--a035d357-e930-5d33-ab8d-d0314092d036","30":"instance--3af551b8-f6ac-5f54-9f6d-403fecdc69eb","300":"instance--298b5d2a-bf93-51e9-b052-19ce36114a5d","330":"instance--c8ea0da0-a19a-5766-b0d1-8524844a59d1","60":"instance--a204f87d-ace7-5a9e-b3d1-13202bdc5c7b","90":"instance--fff4de11-3f84-52c8-bb77-192210612a62"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--12","properties":[["name","Exploit exposed Docker API"],["description","Port 2375 gets the Docker API exploit, creating a privileged container with the host root mounted:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0004","technique":"T1611"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--cac05670-e90e-512c-99cc-c0adf909c3ef","120":"instance--43922820-ddd3-5742-a88d-49c20f8e3fd5","150":"instance--884271a6-8d7b-5c96-9ece-61be4126898b","180":"instance--373a94ef-653d-5c24-96f7-d0cf326d3aea","210":"instance--e58b782a-e75e-5141-bdf0-6d47dbed96bd","240":"instance--5960e46a-3307-5101-b96f-f1bae10e323d","270":"instance--a5ae1125-6ca5-54f1-b9d3-0091a0a38367","30":"instance--e7c521dd-fe09-528b-bb67-1ec53389b876","300":"instance--582e0864-cb5c-5de1-b6c0-e162ae91e8bc","330":"instance--3d5550f3-3e33-5d71-b71e-db2a0a957e5e","60":"instance--b83fc757-0bd4-5b63-a13e-e5b8ef5956d2","90":"instance--2a745819-837b-5585-a366-81a34117a6e5"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--13","properties":[["name","Run payload on remote host"],["description","Both paths deliver the same payload, which runs the Iran timezone check on the remote host. Iranian targets get wiped, everyone else gets the backdoor installed as a systemd service."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0011","technique":"T1105"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--2accaaf8-d071-542e-9a10-06866a96b394","120":"instance--75ef5b2f-7c71-566e-baf2-29f54ced8138","150":"instance--73017f0a-a5f3-5dca-b91c-a2d37bcfe21b","180":"instance--2f1b6e5f-d3b0-59e5-b3c8-6c1399d1ce2a","210":"instance--c7aedd91-3346-5b75-9e3a-842851881a25","240":"instance--2146989b-d8a2-53f0-8a1c-cd3d976227e9","270":"instance--1b0bbd91-fa2a-5897-96d0-9e5918961c9c","30":"instance--e6b73353-364e-5586-a07b-e1fdc92ad2d3","300":"instance--0fdc5473-d5b9-5fed-91a3-21958da6287b","330":"instance--fd1cd9e0-5761-5725-801f-bf88b65914e8","60":"instance--a58b8357-6abc-58d7-ad2b-bec48fffcd9b","90":"instance--e8daf33f-0240-5544-9f99-3be7ac96fc1d"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--14","properties":[["name","Wipe remote host with rm and reboot"],["description","The wiper itself changed. The earlier versions used on non-K8s hosts, while the DaemonSet variant used with a forced reboot. This version standardises on the approach with across the board:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0040","technique":"T1485"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--c80ca3ef-db0a-5372-968e-c17eb31a79ca","120":"instance--69989f45-927f-57be-92e5-5102fccd9f11","150":"instance--9b02c549-b183-5406-a100-249fb1868d16","180":"instance--c1d2a890-ed8d-5123-92d5-ceeaa937ee87","210":"instance--b785b7b9-02d5-5d04-be0c-0d02d4f85620","240":"instance--cde2d3fb-a23f-5188-9d7d-6c7f3cd3cebb","270":"instance--3fa59d94-25bb-5c51-af21-1a7c1fd91f66","30":"instance--fdd04191-1a03-5134-b88e-a55240471931","300":"instance--dddeb587-c160-5bdc-a385-f5d294f11e92","330":"instance--a13b6b46-2b8e-5660-b86f-03747a07fe24","60":"instance--d996db22-4d65-536a-83bf-a1db02b37136","90":"instance--258e2cac-1806-5147-8d61-a10d64a86e46"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--15","properties":[["name","Install renamed systemd service"],["description","A few other changes from the previous versions: the service name moved from to , the install path moved from to , and the systemd description is now \"Postgres Monitor Service\". The PostgreSQL camouflage is getting more consistent."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1543.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--35652c79-2c41-5d60-81ba-b5e47aa554bf","120":"instance--53906203-fffb-5af3-b112-44a9b4b49b8f","150":"instance--465fbc8a-7b4c-569f-be00-c0fbc137fcfc","180":"instance--a653c96b-3673-5dfa-968e-188fffe4cc04","210":"instance--6a344cf5-bd5c-52db-84f5-23c7701c7a5e","30":"instance--913561d1-b5f3-54d2-8272-159233dfde54","330":"instance--d59fe52d-c897-5f3a-919a-c2273cb8a8b3","60":"instance--f1fd6a3d-bb83-543d-a379-39d4632978f7","90":"instance--4cd6fce2-0d24-57f0-b161-12a867cd1100","branch:False":"instance--f7e897b3-3607-5ea5-8d15-5f83ba8a60da","branch:True":"instance--39b5ac19-b0dd-5674-a7d9-d75e